 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "For questions 6 and 7, use the following situation and graph:\n<blockquote>\nElena is considering buying bracelets and necklaces as gifts for her friends. Bracelets, <span data-math=\"b\">b</span>,&nbsp; cost $3, and necklaces, <span data-math=\"n\">n</span>, cost $5. She can spend no more than $30 on the gifts. Elena needs at least 7 gift items.<br> This graph represents the inequality <span data-math=\"3b+5n≤30\">3b+5n≤30</span>, which describes the cost constraint in this situation. <br> <img alt=\"Graph of inequality. Number of necklaces. Number of bracelets.\n&nbsp;\" class=\"img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"234\" src=\"exercises/media/f356a2bd162bf11b.svg\" width=\"315\">    </blockquote>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 646414,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"6\">\n    <li>Let <span data-math=\"b\">b</span> represent the number of bracelets and <span data-math=\"n\">n</span> the number of necklaces.<br> Which inequality represents the number of gift items that Elena needs?</li>\n  </ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1272616,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"b+n=7\">b+n=7</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1272617,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"b+n<7\">b+n&lt;7</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1272618,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"b+n≥7\">b+n≥7</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1272619,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"b+n>7\">b+n&gt;7</span>"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 646415,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"7\">\n  <li>Which of the following could be solutions to the system of inequalities? Select <strong>two</strong> answers.</li>\n</ol>\n<ol type=\"a\">\n  <li><span data-math=\"(8,5)\">(8,5)</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"(1,5)\">(1,5)</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"(7,1)\">(7,1)</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"(6,2)\">(6,2)</span></li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [],
